// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu3, chess
//
// The checked-in aie_trace.mlir no longer parses: aie.trace.host_config has
// since changed assembly format, so the `buffer_size = ... arg_idx = ...`
// trailer is read as a separate op and aiecc fails with
//   aie_trace.mlir:161:29: error: Dialect `' not found for custom op
//   'buffer_size'
// Pre-existing breakage in the example, unrelated to wiring it into lit; it
// was simply never exercised before. Regenerating aie_trace.mlir from
// aie_trace.py against the current trace API should fix it.
// XFAIL: *
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu3
// RUN: cd test_npu3
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile all
// RUN: %run_on_npu3% make -f %S/Makefile run
